course: dictionary
lesson: 8056
title: Using context clues: reindeer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about a real animal, and some are about a story. Context tells you which. «Reindeer, called caribou in North America, have broad hooves for snow and ice.» The words snow, ice and caribou show you that reindeer are animals that live in cold places.
explain: «In Frozen, Sven the reindeer begs for carrots.» In a film, a reindeer can talk and act like a person. The clue is the word Frozen, which names a film. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then check your answer against the words around it.
explain: One word can point to two different things. «Reindeer pull Santa's flying sleigh» is from a Christmas story. «Reindeer have thick fur and large branched antlers» is a fact about the real animal. Read the words around the word to see which one the writer means.
fact: A reindeer is a deer that lives in the cold Arctic and northern lands.
fact: Reindeer have thick fur and large branched antlers.
fact: In North America, wild reindeer are called caribou.
fact: In Christmas stories, reindeer pull Santa's flying sleigh, led by Rudolph with his red nose.
fact: Unlike other deer, both males and females usually grow antlers.
exercise: «Reindeer, called caribou in North America, have broad hooves for snow and ice.» Where do reindeer live? | Warm tropical forests | *Cold Arctic and northern lands | Dry, sandy beaches | Hot desert lands
exercise: «Reindeer dig through the snow with their broad hooves to eat lichen.» What does broad mean here? | Soft and warm | Very sharp | Hidden | *Wide
exercise: Tom says, «Reindeer pull Santa's flying sleigh.» Is he talking about a real animal or a story? | A type of boat | Real animal in Arctic snow | *Christmas story | A dinosaur
test: «Both males and females grow antlers, unlike other deer.» What are antlers? | *Large branched horns on the head | Long tails | Soft, furry ears | Thick fur on the legs
test: In North America, wild reindeer are called what? | Bison | Moose | Elk | *Caribou
exam: Which clue in «In Frozen, Sven the reindeer begs for carrots» shows that Sven is from a film, not real life? | carrots | the reindeer | *In Frozen | Sven
